    "text": "The question that no executioner in the Holy Roman Empire ever recorded an answer to is this: At what point during the vertical bisection of a living human body does consciousness end? The method was reserved for crimes beyond ordinary treason. The condemned was stripped, bound at the ankles, and suspended upside down from a wooden frame. A large two-handled saw was positioned at the groin. Two executioners began pulling the blade downward through the center of the body.",
